SAP in its current form addresses individual query-response alignment. Extended work will develop SAP for multi-turn conversation, long-horizon agentic tasks, and multi-agent structural coordination — where the D-layer conditioning must be maintained across many interaction steps without semantic drift.
10.2 Structure-Driven Agents
Building agents whose internal state is entirely structural rather than goal-based: agents that do not pursue objectives but resolve structural tension, and whose behavior is therefore predictable from their structural configuration rather than from their instruction set.
10.3 Structural Compute Estimation
Predicting compute usage directly from structural density and mismatch, prior to generation. If TC ∝ α·S + β·depth(D) holds across a sufficient range of models and structural configurations, it becomes possible to estimate compute budget from structural input before any generation occurs — a structural resource allocation framework with direct practical applications.
10.4 Worldline Engine Integration
A generalized version of WGL that uses structural vectors as its primary input, replacing or supplementing personal cosmological data with formally specified D-layer configurations. This extends the structural generation framework from individual cognition to collective and systemic worldline prediction.


